This is the software that replaced the org chart.

4
00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:16.947
Every obvious feature — assignment, approval, escalation — was a manager wearing a different name.

5
00:00:16.948 --> 00:00:20.369
The job was saying no to each one.

6
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:25.331
Commitments instead of assignments; read access as the feature.

7
00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:28.690
Eight modules on one object model.

8
00:00:28.691 --> 00:00:34.586
The client is under NDA; the screens are labelled reconstructions.

9
00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:42.364
When the user base and the org chart are the same people, every design call is an org-design call.

10
00:00:43.486 --> 00:00:48.788
Coordination for two hundred people with zero managers in the loop.

11
00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:54.830
The company has since grown to two hundred and fifty — and still runs on it.

12
00:00:54.831 --> 00:01:01.146
Product and design lead across four engineering streams and a PM.

13
00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:10.556
Where this breaks: this only holds where the organisation has genuinely committed to self-management.

14
00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:15.212
The tool can't create that commitment — only carry it.

15
